          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Bob and Mary are standing in a queue. Between Bob and Mary, there are 8 people. Bob sees 18 people including Mary behind him, and Mary sees 14 people including Bob in front of her.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "How many people are in the queue?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$24$ people.\n\nAdd the two counts and subtract the 8 people counted twice.",
      "worked": "Let $X$ be the people behind Bob and $Y$ the people in front of Mary. The 8 people between them belong to both sets. Their union includes everyone in the queue, including Bob and Mary.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}|X\\cup Y|&=|X|+|Y|-|X\\cap Y|\\\\|X\\cup Y|&=18+14-8\\\\|X\\cup Y|&=24\\end{align*}$$\n\nThere are 24 people in the queue.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
